n>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals 328\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>328</mn></math>. Therefore, the graphs of the equations in the given system intersect at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 9 comma 328 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>328</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"1b6bf314-ce44-468e-8236-7d3efe7c0c5f","correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1776362727992,"updateDate":1776362727992}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362727992, 1776362727992),
    ($SATQ$fc3d783a$SATQ$, $SATQ$8acbff18-5c28-43c6-85f6-a6d5078b92cd$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$2c1b597b-7b1d-417b-86b2-1452c25fa720$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables $SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>In the <math><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mi>y</mi>
</mrow>
