pan> by <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fc3dfa26/img_009_305278cd.png\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator x plus 3, and denominator x plus 3, end fraction\"></span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fc3dfa26/img_010_f7de3b7e.png\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator x plus 3, and denominator x squared minus 9, end fraction\"></span>. Therefore, the given equation can be written as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fc3dfa26/img_011_e87cb64e.png\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator 4 x squared, and denominator x squared minus 9, minus, the fraction with numerator 2 x squared, minus 6 x, and denominator x squared minus 9, end fraction, equals, the fraction with numerator x plus 3, and denominator x squared minus 9, end fraction\"></span>. Multiplying each fraction by the denominator results in the equation <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fc3dfa26/img_012_9c22484c.png\" alt=\"4 x squared minus, open parenthesis, 2 x squared, minus 6 x, close parenthesis, equals, x plus 3\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fc3dfa26/img_013_8b26a881.png\" alt=\"2 x squared, plus 6 x, equals, x plus 3\"></span>. This equation can be solved by setting a quadratic expression equal to 0, then solving for <span class=\"italic\">x</span>. Subtracting <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fc3dfa26/img_014_12ebcbad.png\" alt=\"x plus 3 \"></span> from both sides of this equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fc3dfa26/img_015_89658f02.png\" alt=\"2 x squared, plus 5 x, minus 3, equals 0\"></span>. The expression <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fc3dfa26/img_016_676f832d.png\" alt=\"2 x squared, plus 5 x, minus 3 \"></span> can be factored, resulting in the equation <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fc3dfa26/img_017_a0fc8d85.png\" alt=\"open parenthesis, 2 x minus 1, close parenthesis, times, open parenthesis, x plus 3, close parenthesis, equals 0\"></span>. By the zero product property, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fc3dfa26/img_018_f88ec597.png\" alt=\"2 x minus 1, equals 0\"></span> or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fc3dfa26/img_019_e808fc6d.png\" alt=\"x plus 3, equals 0\"></span>. To solve for <span class=\"italic\">x</span> in <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fc3dfa26/img_020_f88ec597.png\" alt=\"2 x minus 1, equals 0\"></span>, 1 can be added to both sides of the equation, resulting in <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=