$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">If the ordered pair <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fcdf87b7/img_001_9121b432.png" alt="x comma y"></span></span> satisfies the system of equations above, what is one possible value of <span class="italic">x</span> ?</p>
$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["either 0","3"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="direction_paragraph ">The correct answer is either 0 or 3. For an ordered pair to satisfy a system of equations, both the <span class="italic">x</span>- and <span class="italic">y</span>-values of the ordered pair must satisfy each equation in the system. Both expressions on the right-hand side of the given equations are equal to <span class="italic">y</span>, therefore it follows that both expressions on the right-hand side of the equations are equal to each other: <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fcdf87b7/img_002_4dc153d8.png" alt="x squared, minus 4 x, plus 4, equals, 4 minus x"></span>. This equation can be rewritten as <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fcdf87b7/img_003_f7e3cf13.png" alt="x squared, minus 3 x, equals 0"></span>, and then through factoring, the equation becomes <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fcdf87b7/img_004_50e4c785.png" alt="x times, open parenthesis, x minus 3, close parenthesis, equals 0"></span>. Because the product of the two factors is equal to 0, it can be concluded that either <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fcdf87b7/img_005_3f34714f.png" alt="x equals 0"></span> or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fcdf87b7/img_006_01515e35.png" alt="x minus 3, equals 0"></span>, or rather, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fcdf87b7/img_007_3f34714f.png" alt="x equals 0"></span> or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fcdf87b7/img_008_6ec6a793.png" alt="x equals 3"></span>. Note that 0 and 3 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>
