    ($SATQ$ffdfe1e1$SATQ$, $SATQ$2d05a911-7298-4d94-ad93-ec0fefdedb1d$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">There are <math alttext="240"><mn>240</mn>
</math> players in a tennis competition that includes <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> rounds of matches. Each player in the competition will play a match against another player in round <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>. At the end of each round, the player who loses the match is eliminated and the player who won the match advances to the next round to play a match against another winning player. Which equation gives the number of players, <math alttext="p"><mi>p</mi>
</math>, eliminated at the end of round <math alttext="r"><mi>r</mi>
</math>, where <math alttext="r less than or equals 4"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"9137517c-4eea-4f71-9b70-cd2c2c4da721","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p equals 15 left parenthesis one half right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>r</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"2454cd01-1d7b-425c-82b1-1fe7a649f6a8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p equals 15 left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mi>r</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"5a6eaa50-4775-4e08-9683-55f7ccb929eb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p equals 240 left parenthesis one half right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>r</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"95b50aa5-2613-4599-b460-4fc8f975ec86","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p equals 240 left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mi>r</mi></msup></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["5a6eaa50-4775-4e08-9683-55f7ccb929eb"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. It&rsquo;s given that one of the two players in a match is eliminated during each round. Therefore, the number of players decreases by half at the end of each round, and so the number of players eliminated at the end of a round also decreases by half. A decreasing exponential equation can be written in the form <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="p equals a left parenthesis 1 minus b right parenthesis Superscript r"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math> is the value of the decrease each round, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a"><mi>a</mi></math> is the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="p"><mi>p</mi></math>, the number of players, when <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r equals 0"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. It's given that there are <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="240"><mn>240</mn></math> players in the tennis competition. Therefore, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a equals 240"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn></math>. Since the number of players eliminated at the end of a round decreases by half, it follows that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b equals one half"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="240"><mn>240</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="one half"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math> in the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="p equals a left parenthesis 1 minus b right parenthesis Superscript r"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="p equals 240 left parenthesis 1 minus one half right parenthesis Superscript r"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="p equals 240 left parenthesis one half right parenthesis Superscript r"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This equation gives the number of players eliminated at the end of round <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> for a competition in which there are <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="15"><mn>15</mn></math>, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="240"><mn>240</mn></math>, players.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This equation gives the number of players eliminated at the end of round <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> for a competition in which there are <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="15"><mn>15</mn></math>, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="240"><mn>240</mn></math>, players, and for which the number of players doubles, rather than decreases by half, after each round.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This equation gives the number of players eliminated at the end of round <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> for a competition in which the number of players doubles, rather than decreases by half, after each round.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"ffdfe1e1","external_id":"2d05a911-7298-4d94-ad93-ec0fefdedb1d","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"354a401b-96f6-458f-ac28-932ff2844604","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">There are <math alttext=\"240\"><mn>240</mn>\n</math> players in a tennis competition that includes <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> rounds of matches. Each player in the competition will play a match against another player in round <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>. At the end of each round, the player who loses the match is eliminated and the player who won the match advances to the next round to play a match against another winning player. Which equation gives the number of players, <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math>, eliminated at the end of round <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"r less than or equals 4\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"9137517c-4eea-4f71-9b70-cd2c2c4da721","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p equals 15 left parenthesis one half right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>r</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"2454cd01-1d7b-425c-82b1-1fe7a649f6a8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p equals 15 left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mi>r</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"5a6eaa50-4775-4e08-9683-55f7ccb929eb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p equals 240 left parenthesis one half right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>r</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"95b50aa5-2613-4599-b460-4fc8f975ec86","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p equals 240 left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mi>r</mi></msup></math></p>"}],"keys":["5a6eaa50-4775-4e08-9683-55f7ccb929eb"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. It&rsquo;s given that one of the two players in a match is eliminated during each round. Therefore, the number of players decreases by half at the end of each round, and so the number of players eliminated at the end of a round also decreases by half. A decreasing exponential equation can be written in the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p equals a left parenthesis 1 minus b right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> is the value of the decrease each round, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math> is the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi></math>, the number of players, when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r equals 0\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. It's given that there are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"240\"><mn>240</mn></math> players in the tennis competition. Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a equals 240\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn></math>. Since the number of players eliminated at the end of a round decreases by half, it follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b equals one half\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"240\"><mn>240</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"one half\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> in the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p equals a left parenthesis 1 minus b right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p equals 240 left parenthesis 1 minus one half right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p equals 240 left parenthesis one half right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This equation gives the number of players eliminated at the end of round <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> for a competition in which there are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"240\"><mn>240</mn></math>, players.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This equation gives the number of players eliminated at the end of round <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> for a competition in which there are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"240\"><mn>240</mn></math>, players, and for which the number of players doubles, rather than decreases by half, after each round.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This equation gives the number of players eliminated at the end of round <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> for a competition in which the number of players doubles, rather than decreases by half, after each round.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1776362727992,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"ffdfe1e1","skill_cd":"P.C.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","createDate":1776362727992,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"","external_id":"2d05a911-7298-4d94-ad93-ec0fefdedb1d","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"354a401b-96f6-458f-ac28-932ff2844604","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">There are <math alttext=\"240\"><mn>240</mn>\n</math> players in a tennis competition that includes <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> rounds of matches. Each player in the competition will play a match against another player in round <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>. At the end of each round, the player who loses the match is eliminated and the player who won the match advances to the next round to play a match against another winning player. Which equation gives the number of players, <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math>, eliminated at the end of round <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"r less than or equals 4\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>?</p>","keys":["5a6eaa50-4775-4e08-9683-55f7ccb929eb"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"9137517c-4eea-4f71-9b70-cd2c2c4da721","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p equals 15 left parenthesis one half right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>r</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"2454cd01-1d7b-425c-82b1-1fe7a649f6a8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p equals 15 left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mi>r</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"5a6eaa50-4775-4e08-9683-55f7ccb929eb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p equals 240 left parenthesis one half right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>r</mi></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"95b50aa5-2613-4599-b460-4fc8f975ec86","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p equals 240 left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mi>r</mi></msup></math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. It&rsquo;s given that one of the two players in a match is eliminated during each round. Therefore, the number of players decreases by half at the end of each round, and so the number of players eliminated at the end of a round also decreases by half. A decreasing exponential equation can be written in the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p equals a left parenthesis 1 minus b right parenthesis Superscript r\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math