<p style="text-align: left;">The table shows the distribution of two types of flowers at two different sites. If a flower represented in the table is selected at random, what is the probability of selecting a flower from site A, given that the flower is a tulip? (Express your answer as a decimal or fraction, not as a percent.)</p>$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["0.7","7/10"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["0.7","7/10"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 35 Over 50 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>35</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac></math>. Based on the table, there are a total of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="50"><mn>50</mn></math> tulips, and&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="35"><mn>35</mn></math> of these tulips are from site A. The probability of selecting at random a flower from site A, given that the flower is a tulip, is equal to the number of tulips from site A divided by the total number of tulips, which can be written as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 35 Over 50 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>35</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="seven tenths"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math>. Note that 35/50, 7/10, and .7&nbsp;are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"014c47ab","external_id":"3bdb04eb-289a-4c97-b759-9893b1508252","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"b5aee5f6-6347-4f7f-986b-1b5d3c8c34a4","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.E.","skill_desc":"Probability and conditional probability","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<figure class=\"table\"><table border=\"1\">\n<thea